  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What is compared with what",
      "items": [
        "Cards vs the route inventory, the JUnit report, the live store and the files their evidence names; contracts vs real components rendered per state",
        "Sources are never parsed — only what the system states about itself; in the package only scaffold reads an OpenAPI document, for drafts and never for verdicts; a route inventory may be made from one outside it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "What the box holds",
      "items": [
        "Six commands: validate and check run in the gates, conformance runs the corpus; scaffold drafts cards from an OpenAPI document, gen openapi writes one from the cards, preview draws contracts as a wireframe page",
        "Six schemas: card and contract are read at run time by both checkers; the other four describe the config and the three inventories"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Two readings, one corpus",
      "items": [
        "TypeScript reference and Python prototype must report the same codes on 152 cases",
        "A deliberately rotten repository must still fail, and CI compares what both checkers report on it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Where it runs",
      "items": [
        "npx usedesign@<pin> in each product's CI — nothing installed, version frozen per repository; each gate runs validate, then check; the frontend gate reads the server's cards via a sibling checkout",
        "Publish is green only when the registry actually serves the box",
        "The starter kit (Russian) is the copy-and-go path: a sample config and gate, a script for the route inventory, a recipe test for the form inventory"
      ]
    }
  ]
